WEBVTT

00:00.840 --> 00:02.040
Matthew 18

00:02.040 --> 00:06.820
At that time the disciples came to Jesus, saying,

00:07.600 --> 00:09.780
Who is the greatest in the kingdom of heaven?

00:10.040 --> 00:15.660
And calling to him a child, he put him in the midst of them and said,

00:16.480 --> 00:22.520
Truly I say to you, unless you turn and become like children, you will never enter the kingdom of heaven.

00:23.140 --> 00:27.760
Whoever humbles himself like this child is the greatest in the kingdom of heaven.

00:27.760 --> 00:32.340
Whoever receives one such child in my name receives me.

00:33.000 --> 00:37.100
But whoever causes one of these little ones who believe in me to sin,

00:37.560 --> 00:42.400
it would be better for him to have a great millstone fastened around his neck

00:42.400 --> 00:44.760
and to be drowned in the depth of the sea.

00:46.120 --> 00:51.620
Woe to the world for temptations to sin, for it is necessary that temptations come.

00:52.120 --> 00:55.140
But woe to the one by whom the temptation comes.

00:55.540 --> 00:57.640
And if your hand or your foot...

00:57.760 --> 01:01.300
If your foot causes you to sin, cut it off and throw it away.

01:01.820 --> 01:04.700
It is better for you to enter life crippled or lame

01:04.700 --> 01:08.640
than with two hands or two feet to be thrown into the eternal fire.

01:09.400 --> 01:13.380
And if your eye causes you to sin, tear it out and throw it away.

01:13.960 --> 01:16.720
It is better for you to enter life with one eye

01:16.720 --> 01:19.960
than with two eyes to be thrown into the hell of fire.

01:21.060 --> 01:24.140
See that you do not despise one of these little ones.

01:24.140 --> 01:27.140
For I tell you that in heaven their angels...

01:27.760 --> 01:29.940
I see the face of my Father who is in heaven.

01:30.740 --> 01:31.720
What do you think?

01:32.080 --> 01:35.340
If a man has a hundred sheep and one of them has gone astray,

01:35.780 --> 01:38.100
does he not leave the ninety-nine on the mountains

01:38.100 --> 01:40.720
and go in search of the one that went astray?

01:41.800 --> 01:44.780
And if he finds it, truly I say to you,

01:45.020 --> 01:49.120
he rejoices over it more than over the ninety-nine that never went astray.

01:49.900 --> 01:53.080
So it is not the will of my Father who is in heaven

01:53.080 --> 01:55.920
that one of these little ones should perish.

01:56.880 --> 01:57.600
If your...

01:57.600 --> 01:58.960
If your brother sins against you,

01:59.420 --> 02:02.360
go and tell him his fault, between you and him alone.

02:02.900 --> 02:05.580
If he listens to you, you have gained your brother.

02:06.220 --> 02:09.740
But if he does not listen, take one or two others along with you,

02:09.940 --> 02:13.820
that every charge may be established by the evidence of two or three witnesses.

02:14.520 --> 02:18.220
If he refuses to listen to them, tell it to the church.

02:18.840 --> 02:21.460
And if he refuses to listen even to the church,

02:21.600 --> 02:24.860
let him be to you as a Gentile and a tax collector.

02:26.220 --> 02:27.580
Truly I say to you,

02:27.580 --> 02:30.300
whatever you bind on earth shall be bound in heaven,

02:30.580 --> 02:33.620
and whatever you loose on earth shall be loosed in heaven.

02:34.320 --> 02:35.700
Again I say to you,

02:36.000 --> 02:38.780
if two of you agree on earth about anything they ask,

02:39.020 --> 02:41.320
it will be done for them by my Father in heaven.

02:41.900 --> 02:44.300
For where two or three are gathered in my name,

02:44.860 --> 02:46.320
there am I among them.

02:47.960 --> 02:49.780
Then Peter came up and said to him,

02:50.360 --> 02:54.800
Lord, how often will my brother sin against me and I forgive him?

02:55.080 --> 02:57.560
As many as seven times?

02:58.400 --> 02:59.640
Jesus said to him,

03:00.400 --> 03:04.740
I do not say to you seven times, but seventy times seven.

03:05.720 --> 03:08.800
Therefore the kingdom of heaven may be compared to a king

03:08.800 --> 03:10.860
who wished to settle accounts with his servants.

03:11.640 --> 03:13.160
When he began to settle,

03:13.580 --> 03:16.580
one was brought to him who owed him ten thousand talents.

03:17.240 --> 03:18.580
And since he could not pay,

03:18.900 --> 03:22.260
his master ordered him to be sold with his wife and children

03:22.260 --> 03:24.500
and all that he had in payment to be made.

03:25.300 --> 03:27.100
So the servant fell on his knees,

03:27.100 --> 03:28.020
imploring him,

03:28.440 --> 03:29.800
Have patience with me,

03:30.040 --> 03:31.520
and I will pay you everything.

03:32.560 --> 03:33.760
And out of pity for him,

03:34.020 --> 03:35.940
the master of that servant released him

03:35.940 --> 03:37.380
and forgave him the debt.

03:38.040 --> 03:39.960
But when that same servant went out,

03:40.300 --> 03:41.880
he found one of his fellow servants

03:41.880 --> 03:43.960
who owed him a hundred denarii,

03:44.220 --> 03:45.500
and seizing him,

03:45.720 --> 03:47.360
he began to choke him, saying,

03:47.700 --> 03:48.580
Pay what you owe.

03:48.980 --> 03:51.800
So his fellow servant fell down and pleaded with him,

03:52.180 --> 03:53.480
Have patience with me,

03:53.660 --> 03:54.860
and I will pay you.

03:55.420 --> 03:56.460
He refused,

03:56.460 --> 03:56.540
and refused,

03:56.540 --> 03:56.620
and refused,

03:56.620 --> 03:56.640
and refused,

03:56.640 --> 03:56.680
and refused,

03:56.680 --> 03:56.720
and refused,

03:56.720 --> 03:56.800
and refused,

03:56.800 --> 03:56.820
and refused,

03:56.820 --> 03:56.840
and refused,

03:56.840 --> 03:57.080
and refused,

03:57.100 --> 03:58.220
and went and put him in prison

03:58.220 --> 03:59.760
until he should pay the debt.

04:00.340 --> 04:03.180
When his fellow servants saw what had taken place,

04:03.440 --> 04:05.240
they were greatly distressed,

04:05.640 --> 04:07.820
and they went and reported to their master

04:07.820 --> 04:09.340
all that had taken place.

04:10.440 --> 04:13.040
Then his master summoned him and said to him,

04:13.560 --> 04:14.960
You wicked servant,

04:15.260 --> 04:17.060
I forgave you all that debt

04:17.060 --> 04:18.580
because you pleaded with me,

04:19.040 --> 04:20.760
and should not you have had mercy

04:20.760 --> 04:21.940
on your fellow servant

04:21.940 --> 04:23.940
as I had mercy on you?

04:24.800 --> 04:27.080
And in anger his master delivered,

04:27.080 --> 04:27.120
And in anger his master delivered,

04:27.120 --> 04:28.260
and delivered him to the jailers,

04:28.260 --> 04:30.640
until he should pay all his debt.

04:30.640 --> 04:31.240
until he should pay all his debt.

04:31.240 --> 04:31.700
But he did not even fall for your lies,

04:31.700 --> 04:32.320
and will ever prevent you

04:32.320 --> 04:32.460
And he did not even fall for your lies,

04:32.460 --> 04:33.420
although he had enough

04:33.420 --> 04:34.120
and also my heavenly father

04:34.120 --> 04:35.880
will do to every one of you

04:35.880 --> 04:38.540
if you do not forgive your brother

04:38.540 --> 04:39.660
from your heart.

04:39.840 --> 04:50.060
How will you forgive him?

04:52.360 --> 04:55.060
Whether you forgive his brother

04:55.060 --> 04:57.060
By loving him

